If you're designing Terraform for a production environment, there are several patterns beyond "list vs dictionary" that can significantly affect maintainability, safety, and scalability.

1. count vs for_each
❌ Bad

count = length(var.instances)
✅ Better

for_each = var.instances
Use for_each whenever resources have a unique identity.

Examples

S3 buckets

IAM users

IAM roles

Security Groups

Route53 records

ECR repositories

SNS Topics

Use count only when resources are identical.

Example

count = 3
Three identical EC2 instances.

2. List vs Map
❌

[
  "prod",
  "uat",
  "dev"
]
✅

{
  prod = {}
  uat = {}
  dev = {}
}
Maps provide stable identities.

3. Primitive variables vs Object variables
❌

