Production Terraform Design Principles
Principle    Recommendation
Resource identity    for_each + map over count + list
Configuration    Prefer object and map(object) over many primitive variables
Code reuse    Build small, focused modules
State    Split by domain or lifecycle; use a remote backend
Naming    Use locals and conventions, avoid hardcoding
Security    Never store secrets in code or state if avoidable
Validation    Validate inputs early with validation blocks
Safety    Use prevent_destroy and other lifecycle controls where appropriate
Portability    Avoid hardcoded IDs, ARNs, regions, and AMIs
Maintainability    Keep modules cohesive, versioned, and documented
These are the patterns typically enforced in mature Terraform codebases supporting dozens of AWS accounts, hundreds of modules, and multiple engineering teams.


