Once you reach 100+ microservices, Helm stops being a packaging tool and becomes a configuration management platform. Most failures are not due to Helm itself—they come from poor repository structure, uncontrolled configuration drift, and weak release governance.

Below are the design patterns used in large-scale organizations (banks, telecoms, SaaS platforms).

1. Application vs Microservice Separation
Never create one giant chart.

❌

banking-app/

    Chart.yaml

    templates/

        frontend

        backend

        auth

        payment

        ledger

        notification

        ...
Every deployment upgrades everything.

Instead

charts/

    auth/

    payment/

    ledger/

    notification/

applications/

    retail-banking/

    corporate-banking/

    credit-card/
Application becomes orchestration.

2. App-of-Apps Pattern
Retail Banking

├── auth 2.1.3
├── payment 5.2.8
├── notification 3.0.4
├── ledger 8.1.2
